Hint:"Once enabled, when you ask her to do something in chat she can read the current screen and tap, type or go back for you.",settingsAgentDisabled:"Not enabled yet.",settingsAgentEnabledNotConnected:"Enabled in system settings, but the service is not running yet — switch back to the app and try again.",settingsAgentConnected:"Enabled and ready.",settingsAgentOpenSettings:"Enable",settingsAgentOpenSettingsAgain:"Open system settings",settingsAgentTest:"Read the current screen",settingsAgentTestCrossApp:"Take a trip to system settings",settingsAgentCrossResult:"Opened {pkg}, read {n} controls",settingsAgentCrossNoTarget:"Found nothing to tap.",settingsAgentCrossTapped:"Tapped “{label}” — now in {pkg} (page: {heading})",settingsAgentCrossFailed:"Could not open system settings.",settingsAgentTapFailed:"The tap did not go through.",settingsAgentTesting:"Reading…",settingsAgentOpenFailed:"Could not open system settings. Go to Settings → Accessibility and find Sweetheart.",settingsAgentPrivacy:"She only reads the screen when you ask her to. Nothing about what you open or see is recorded in the background.",settingsAgentOverlayTitle:"Coming back to the chat",settingsAgentOverlayHint:'After she runs an errand in another app she needs to bring her own screen back to the front. Android ties that ability to "Display over other apps" (the system only accepts that switch —it does not mean she floats on your screen). Without it she can still work, you just have to switch back yourself.',settingsAgentOverlayOn:"on",settingsAgentOverlayOff:"off",settingsAgentOverlayOpen:"Turn this on",settingsAgentNotifyTitle:"Calling you back",settingsAgentNotifyHint:"Android does not let an app jump back to the foreground by itself, so when she finishes an errand in another app she sends a notification to call you back. Without it the work still gets done — you just will not hear her say she is back.",settingsAgentNotifyOpen:"Allow notifications",agentMode:"Access",agentModeChat:"Chat only",age